Section: Name resolver
  cdx-duplicate-definition : Integer = 3001

  cdx-undefined-name : Integer = 3002

  cdx-duplicate-cite : Integer = 3003

  cdx-chapter-pagination : Integer = 3004

  cdx-shadows-builtin : Integer = 3005

  cdx-collides-across-chapters : Integer = 3006

  cdx-missing-cite : Integer = 3010

 3010 is the build resolver's condition: the chapter is not on disk under
 the quire it was cited from. 3007 is a different one -- the file may exist
 and resolve perfectly well, but this particular compilation unit was
 assembled without it. A tool that cites Foreword chapter Console and is
 concatenated without Console.codex is the second and not the first. They
 are separate codes because they have separate fixes: correct the name or
 the quire for 3010, include the chapter or drop the cite for 3007.

 3007 is a WARNING, and deliberately. Measured when it was first written as
 an error: it halts the sign tool's build, because that tool cites Console
 and its unit does not carry it. Whether each such cite is a real defect or
 a harmless leftover is exactly what nobody has measured, and shipping it as
 an error would have decided that question by breaking the build.

  cdx-cite-not-in-unit : Integer = 3007

